---
description: Phoenix Security (ASPM) workflows — apply when the task involves security posture, assets, vulnerabilities, findings, CVEs, remediation, exploitability, or risk of applications/teams.
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the `phoenix-security` MCP tools (`phoenix_*`); fall back to the `phx`
CLI (`-o json`) if MCP is unavailable.

Conventions: finding-search severity is 0–1000 (critical ≥ 900, high ≥ 700);
import/write severity is a string "1.0"–"10.0"; EPSS ≥ 0.5 = likely
exploited; default to OPEN findings; keep limits ≤ 100 and summarise rather
than dumping JSON.

Playbooks:
- Find asset: phoenix_search_assets (types INFRA/CLOUD/WEB/CONTAINER/
  REPOSITORY/BUILD/CODE), match key/attributes/tags; detail via
  phoenix_get_asset.
- Find vulnerability: phoenix_search_findings (cves, status ["OPEN"],
  severity_score_from, application_environment_id, team_ids).
- Remediation: phoenix_get_finding → data[].remedy (fix), location,
  parents[] (owning app/component).
- Exploitable now: OPEN + zero_day_alert=true, plus OPEN +
  epss_score_from "0.5"; rank EPSS × severity; flag exposed/EXTERNAL.
- App report: list_applications (resolve name) → get_application_posture →
  list_components(parent_id) → search_assets(application_environment_id) →
  search_findings(...) → summary + remediation shortlist.
- Create/enrich asset: phoenix_create_asset / phoenix_enrich_asset
  (INFRA ip+hostname; CLOUD providerType+providerAccountId; CONTAINER
  dockerfile = image reference e.g. myorg/api:2.0; REPOSITORY repository).
  Safe upsert by attributes.
- Enrich finding: phoenix_enrich_finding (import-merge; needs asset
  attributes + name/description/remedy/severity). From a finding ID: get
  finding → exact data[].name + assetId → get asset → use its attributes;
  a changed name creates a NEW finding.

API v1.27 cannot: change finding status/severity/comments, delete assets or
remove asset tags, delete apps/teams/users, list scanner types. Check
phoenix_api_gaps and state the workaround — never invent endpoints.
